# Wedding Planner — local environment
#
# Copy to `.env` in this folder (same place as package.json), fill in the key,
# then restart `npm run dev`. Vite reads this file only when it starts.
#
# Never commit `.env`. The anon key stays out of git. Netlify project
# baliplanner already has VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.
# A new Netlify build is required after those values change.
#
# Dashboard sign-in is not an email password. Sign in to GitHub as
# v8ws59j2m2-bot with Apple, then on https://supabase.com/dashboard choose
# Sign in with GitHub, and open project gezexfnzemsqhrvizetj.
# Copy the anon / publishable key from Project Settings → API.
# Do not use the service_role key.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://gezexfnzemsqhrvizetj.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The published site does not read VITE_DATA_SOURCE.
# Leave it unset. An uncommitted local experiment uses it. See docs/MAINTENANCE.md.
